      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Why it is used",
      "items": [
        "Three models agreeing is far stronger evidence than one model alone",
        "It is the only tab that exports all models in a single file",
        "It shows which model earned its complexity",
        "It is the tab to screenshot into a client deck"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Read it this way",
      "items": [
        "Agreement under 5% — quote the midpoint as a working forecast",
        "Divergence above 5% — investigate the drivers before quoting anything",
        "Quote a band across the horizon, never a single number",
